{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-53158","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101469","text":"Lane F — finish the reconciliation"}]},{"id":"blk-53159","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101470","marks":["bold"],"text":"Owns:"},{"id":"spn-101471","text":" root "},{"id":"spn-101472","marks":["code"],"text":"*.md"},{"id":"spn-101473","text":", "},{"id":"spn-101474","marks":["code"],"text":"AGENTS.md"},{"id":"spn-101475","text":", "},{"id":"spn-101476","marks":["code"],"text":"agents/"},{"id":"spn-101477","text":" "},{"id":"spn-101478","marks":["bold"],"text":"Must not touch:"},{"id":"spn-101479","text":" "},{"id":"spn-101480","marks":["code"],"text":"computedriven.com/"},{"id":"spn-101481","text":" (lane E), "},{"id":"spn-101482","marks":["code"],"text":"RRABBIT/"},{"id":"spn-101483","text":" (lane A), "},{"id":"spn-101484","marks":["code"],"text":"studbook/"},{"id":"spn-101485","text":" (lane B). "},{"id":"spn-101486","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status: ✅ READY NOW."},{"id":"spn-101487","text":" Unblocked, and it clears debt that is actively misleading other sessions."}]},{"id":"blk-53160","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101488","text":"Why this lane matters more than it looks"}]},{"id":"blk-53161","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101489","text":"On 2026-08-15 "},{"id":"spn-101490","marks":["code"],"text":"CLAUDE.md"},{"id":"spn-101491","text":" — the file injected into "},{"id":"spn-101492","marks":["bold"],"text":"every session in this tree"},{"id":"spn-101493","text":" — was found still teaching the shared-Supabase data layer, with the full migration table and runnable "},{"id":"spn-101494","marks":["code"],"text":"supabase start"},{"id":"spn-101495","text":" commands. It had been abandoned "},{"id":"spn-101496","marks":["bold"],"text":"sixteen days earlier"},{"id":"spn-101497","text":". Every session in that window began from a false premise."}]},{"id":"blk-53162","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101498","marks":["bold"],"text":"That is the failure this lane exists to prevent."},{"id":"spn-101499","text":" A ruling that is not swept into the documents is a ruling the next session does not have."}]},{"id":"blk-53163","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101500","text":"Read first"}]},{"id":"blk-53164","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101501","marks":["code"],"text":"REVISION_REGISTER.md"},{"id":"spn-101502","text":" — the ranked list, with what is fixed and what is not."}]},{"id":"blk-53165","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101503","text":"Still open"}]},{"id":"blk-53166","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101504","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-101505","marks":["code"],"text":"STACK_COMPLETION.md"},{"id":"spn-101506","text":" §0/§6 — "},{"id":"spn-101507","marks":["bold"],"text":"[TRAVIS], not yours"}]},{"id":"blk-53167","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101508","text":"The ratings take Fly deployment breadth as an input, and the wind-down ruling changed it. They are "},{"id":"spn-101509","marks":["bold"],"text":"stale, not wrong"},{"id":"spn-101510","text":". The document already reserves the blended-vs-per-layer question for Travis. "},{"id":"spn-101511","marks":["bold"],"text":"Flag it; do not recompute it."}]},{"id":"blk-53168","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101512","text":"2. "},{"id":"spn-101513","marks":["code"],"text":"AGENTS.md"},{"id":"spn-101514","text":" is stale and nobody has audited it"}]},{"id":"blk-53169","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101515","text":"Found in passing, never swept: it describes WebHost.Systems as "},{"id":"spn-101516","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Convex + Vite/React/Clerk\""},{"id":"spn-101517","text":", while "},{"id":"spn-101518","marks":["code"],"text":"CLAUDE.md"},{"id":"spn-101519","text":" says "},{"id":"spn-101520","marks":["bold"],"text":"Supabase backend + Vite/React/Supabase Auth"},{"id":"spn-101521","text":". One of them is wrong and possibly both. It also predates every 2026-08-15 ruling. "},{"id":"spn-101522","marks":["bold"],"text":"95 lines — read all of it against the tree."}]},{"id":"blk-53170","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101523","text":"3. The per-product "},{"id":"spn-101524","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/"},{"id":"spn-101525","text":" folders were never swept"}]},{"id":"blk-53171","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101526","text":"~14 of them. "},{"id":"spn-101527","marks":["code"],"text":"WebHost.Systems/docs/spec/30_DATA_MODEL_SUPABASE.md"},{"id":"spn-101528","text":" is Supabase "},{"id":"spn-101529","marks":["bold"],"text":"by name"},{"id":"spn-101530","text":", and its v1.0 spec is otherwise the most complete hub design in the portfolio. Others certainly assume Supabase or a Fly deployment."}]},{"id":"blk-53172","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101531","marks":["bold"],"text":"Do not mass-edit."},{"id":"spn-101532","text":" Some of these are dated design records where a supersession banner is the honest fix; others are live guidance that should be corrected. "},{"id":"spn-101533","marks":["bold"],"text":"Tell the two apart, and say which you did."}]},{"id":"blk-53173","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101534","text":"4. Verify "},{"id":"spn-101535","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand-supabase/"},{"id":"spn-101536","text":" is marked archived"}]},{"id":"blk-53174","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101537","text":"It is archived by decision. Nothing has checked that the directory "},{"id":"spn-101538","marks":["italic"],"text":"says so"},{"id":"spn-101539","text":" to someone who opens it."}]},{"id":"blk-53175","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101540","text":"5. Does any live page tell the public it runs on Supabase?"}]},{"id":"blk-53176","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101541","text":"Never checked. Curl the served pages rather than grepping the tree — the local-grep error mode is recorded and has produced a wrong claim here before."}]},{"id":"blk-53177","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101542","text":"6. Write the threat model — "},{"id":"spn-101543","marks":["bold"],"text":"the most valuable thing in this lane"}]},{"id":"blk-53178","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101544","marks":["code"],"text":"CONFIDENTIALITY.md"},{"id":"spn-101545","text":" §1 lists seven adversaries (T1–T7) and "},{"id":"spn-101546","marks":["bold"],"text":"none are declared in scope"},{"id":"spn-101547","text":". Every mechanism choice in class B is downstream of that answer. This is a "},{"id":"spn-101548","marks":["bold"],"text":"[TRAVIS]"},{"id":"spn-101549","text":" ruling, but the document that makes it easy to make — the concrete question, the consequence of each answer — is yours to write."}]},{"id":"blk-53179","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101550","text":"House rules for this lane specifically"}]},{"id":"blk-53180","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53182","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101551","marks":["bold"],"text":"Retract in place, by name."},{"id":"spn-101552","text":" Never silently edit a claim away. This tree's retractions are its"}]}],"id":"blk-53181","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-53183","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101553","text":"most valuable records — the ledger that retracted two of its own findings, the plan that retracted its own pricing twice."}]},{"id":"blk-53184","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53186","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101554","marks":["bold"],"text":"Do not rewrite dated analyses."},{"id":"spn-101555","text":" A gap review records what was seen at the time; rewriting it"}]}],"id":"blk-53185","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-53187","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101556","text":"fabricates a review nobody performed. "},{"id":"spn-101557","marks":["code"],"text":"STACK_ARCHITECTURE_GAP_REVIEW.md"},{"id":"spn-101558","text":", "},{"id":"spn-101559","marks":["code"],"text":"ECOSYSTEM.md"},{"id":"spn-101560","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-101561","marks":["code"],"text":"STACK_PLANNING.md"},{"id":"spn-101562","text":" got "},{"id":"spn-101563","marks":["bold"],"text":"supersession banners"},{"id":"spn-101564","text":" for exactly this reason. Say which half survives."}]},{"id":"blk-53188","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53190","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101565","marks":["bold"],"text":"Never hand-type a derived number."},{"id":"spn-101566","text":" The law count drifted "},{"id":"spn-101567","marks":["bold"],"text":"twice"},{"id":"spn-101568","text":" — 116 in four places in"}]}],"id":"blk-53189","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-53191","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101569","marks":["code"],"text":"STACK_SITEMAP.md"},{"id":"spn-101570","text":" and two more in "},{"id":"spn-101571","marks":["code"],"text":"STACK_COMPLETION.md"},{"id":"spn-101572","text":", where the suites derive "},{"id":"spn-101573","marks":["bold"],"text":"118"},{"id":"spn-101574","text":". The suites count themselves: "},{"id":"spn-101575","marks":["code"],"text":"node test/laws.mjs && node test/compose-laws.mjs"},{"id":"spn-101576","text":" from "},{"id":"spn-101577","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/box-and-box/"},{"id":"spn-101578","text":". Quote the output."}]},{"id":"blk-53192","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53194","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101579","marks":["bold"],"text":"A boundary in a document is a decision, not a measurement."},{"id":"spn-101580","text":" Plan §8.3's out-of-scope list was"}]}],"id":"blk-53193","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-53195","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101581","text":"inherited as fact and produced a conclusion off by four orders of magnitude. If a scope looks load-bearing, ask rather than assume."}]},{"id":"blk-53196","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53198","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101582","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date every claim"},{"id":"spn-101583","text":", and give it the rung it has earned: "},{"id":"spn-101584","marks":["code"],"text":"spec"},{"id":"spn-101585","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-101586","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-101587","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-101588","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-101589","text":" →"}]}],"id":"blk-53197","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-53199","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101590","marks":["code"],"text":"live_deployed"},{"id":"spn-101591","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-101592","marks":["code"],"text":"external"},{"id":"spn-101593","text":". When in doubt, downgrade."}]},{"id":"blk-53200","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101594","text":"Done means"}]},{"id":"blk-53201","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101595","marks":["code"],"text":"REVISION_REGISTER.md"},{"id":"spn-101596","text":" has no open row that is not explicitly "},{"id":"spn-101597","marks":["bold"],"text":"[TRAVIS]"},{"id":"spn-101598","text":", and each closed row says what was done and how it was checked. Keep the register — it is a standing document, not a one-off. The failure it catches is silent and cumulative."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieranzzb57rezssvavgudkirftn6y5ztobsf5ajybth7de4bbcl5mzzq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}